<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syrian Wars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Syrian Wars were a series of conflicts fought between the Ptolemaic and Seleucid kingdoms during the third and second centuries BCE. They centred on control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coele-syria">Coele-Syria</a>, the strategically and commercially valuable territory between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a> identify them as the kingdom's key military conflicts, which drained resources from both Hellenistic dynasties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syrian-wars.jpg" alt="Syrian Wars" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA, earthobservatory, http://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Near_east_lrg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
